--- baseline/exec_bio_text
+++ new/exec_bio_text
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Zahir Uddin is an enterprise IT executive with more than 25 years of experience across life sciences and other regulated industries. He spent over seven years at SK Life Science, Inc., building and running the company's Information Technology function from before its first U.S. product launch through to $1 billion in annual commercial sales. He joined in September 2018 as Enterprise Architect and Commercial Systems Lead, when the IT organization consisted of two people and roughly $3 million in annual spend, and by the time he left in January 2026, as Head of IT (the CIO-equivalent role), had built a SaaS-first, GxP- and SOX-compliant technology environment serving the whole business - manufacturing, R&D, commercial, Finance, Quality, and Supply Chain.
+
+In between, as Vice President, Head of Applications, he led the SAP S/4HANA and Veeva CRM/R&D implementation that made the company's first U.S. launch possible within fourteen months. As Head of IT, he cut IT operating expense by 30% through vendor renegotiation and cloud rightsizing, owned governance for a publicly traded company under K-SOX controls tested annually by PwC, and sponsored practical AI use cases in security operations and Medical Affairs analytics with human review built in throughout. He also led technology diligence and integration for two business acquisitions, including a preclinical company, and owned the Veeva CTMS and eTMF platforms supporting active clinical development.
+
+Earlier in his career he led enterprise data and consulting engagements for organizations including Univision, AbbVie, and Eisai, and managed corporate IT for Kalido's US, UK, France, and India offices. He holds a Bachelor of Science in Information Systems (Artificial Intelligence major, Honours) from Brunel University London and is a Kalido Accredited Consultant and Six Sigma Green Belt.